# Infrastructure (`ForensicsAnalyzer.Infrastructure`)

Implements Application ports. Do not reverse the dependency (Application must not reference this project).

- Persistence: `ApplicationDbContext`, fluent configurations, SQL Server, global filters for `ISoftDelete`.
- Repositories + `UnitOfWork`; register in `DependencyInjection.cs`.
- Identity, JWT, Google OAuth, AutoMapper profiles, development seeders.
- New entity configuration, migration, or NuGet package = architecture-gate question + docs.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — use-case / HTTP in a repository
public async Task<IActionResult> CreateCaseFromHttp(HttpRequest req) { }

// ✅ GOOD — persist only; mapping in profiles; DI in DependencyInjection.cs
```

Migrations and connection strings are persistence changes: explain and ask first. Cover new adapter logic with unit tests (not a live SQL Server unless the user asked for integration tests).
